      "problem": "Let be ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116975/assets/b52c7bab87a334e64abf62ed624ad647145afc894480bd02835bc7b4e678025e.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116975/assets/de8f23ed40b094f2b49b652e42c906ff48e6bd5e078af86c388ef3ebe04016c5.svg) If $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 10\\cdot x+x\\cdot x+0\\cdot 8+5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 10x+{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $x=-5.$",
